-- title:
--   §2.1, pp. 18–23 — partitioned subprobability measures S, the distance d of (2.3), the topology and Borel σ-algebra of (𝒮, d)
-- statement:
--   A **partitioned subprobability measure** is a function $f:\mathbb N\times\mathbb Z^d\to[0,\infty)$ with $\|f\|=\sum_u f(u)\le 1$ (2.1); think of it as a subprobability measure spread over countably many copies $\{n\}\times\mathbb Z^d$ of $\mathbb Z^d$. The set of these is $S$.
--
--   For $u,v\in\mathbb N\times\mathbb Z^d$, $u-v$ is the difference of their sites when they lie on the same copy and $\infty$ otherwise. A map $\phi$ defined on a finite set $A$ is an **isometry of degree $m\ge1$** if $\phi(u)-\phi(v)=u-v$ whenever $u,v\in A$ and either $\|u-v\|_1<m$ or $\|\phi(u)-\phi(v)\|_1<m$ (2.2). For such $\phi$,
--   $$d_\phi(f,g)=2\sum_{u\in A}|f(u)-g(\phi(u))|+\sum_{u\notin A}f(u)^2+\sum_{v\notin\phi(A)}g(v)^2+2^{-\deg\phi},\qquad d(f,g)=\inf_\phi d_\phi(f,g)\quad(2.3).$$
--
--   The quotient $\mathcal S$ of $S$ by $d(f,g)=0$ is the paper's compact metric space. Here $S$ carries the topology generated by the open $d$-balls and its Borel $\sigma$-algebra; the module also provides the zero element, the total mass $\|f\|$, and the embedding of a probability mass function on $\mathbb Z^d$ as an element of $S$ supported on one copy (cf. (3.10)).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The quotient is not formed: by symmetry and the triangle inequality of $d$ (Lemma 2.3) the $d$-balls form a base of the pseudometric topology, every Borel set is saturated, and Borel probability measures on $S$ are exactly those on $\mathcal S$. The weight $2^{-\deg\phi}$ is realised as an infimum over all admissible degrees $m$ of $2^{-m}$ (the degree condition at $m$ implies it at every $m'\le m$), so the infimum over $(A,\phi,m)$ equals the paper's $\inf_\phi d_\phi$. The embedding uses copy $0$; any copy gives the same element of $\mathcal S$ (Corollary 2.5). A function that is not an element of $S$ is mapped to $0$ by the packaging helper.
-- source:
--   Bates and Chatterjee, The endpoint distribution of directed polymers, arXiv:1612.03443v5, pp. 18–23, §2.1, (2.1)–(2.3); p. 29, (3.10)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PolymerEndpoint_GeoLoc_Model
import Definitions.Def_PolymerEndpoint_Atomic_Partitioned

namespace PolymerEndpoint.GeoLoc

open MeasureTheory

/-- The zero element `0`. -/
def zero (d : ℕ) : PolymerEndpoint.Atomic.PSM d :=
  ⟨fun _ => 0, fun _ => le_rfl, summable_zero, by simp⟩

/-- Packages a function as an element of `S` when it is one, and returns `0` otherwise. -/
noncomputable def toPSM {d : ℕ} (g : PolymerEndpoint.Atomic.Cell d → ℝ) : PolymerEndpoint.Atomic.PSM d := by
  classical
  exact if h : (∀ u, 0 ≤ g u) ∧ Summable g ∧ ∑' u, g u ≤ 1 then
    ⟨g, h.1, h.2.1, h.2.2⟩ else zero d

instance instBorelSpacePSM (d : ℕ) : BorelSpace (PolymerEndpoint.Atomic.PSM d) := ⟨rfl⟩

end PolymerEndpoint.GeoLoc


